    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="0725" n="1459" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1459"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-15"><hi rendition="#italic">January 15, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Feb. 3.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 772.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose the copy of a
                    letter just received from Miss Coffing, at Hadjin, which tells of her fears and
                    surroundings. I will at once comply with her requests. My conditional demand for
                    the head of the governor has done good in securing a humane successor for him
                    and in saving Hadjin, thus far, from massacre, while all the surrounding country
                    has suffered and is desolate.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d731-a1.xml" xpointer="d731-a1"/>
